{#
  layouts/redirect.njk — a static redirect stub

  GitHub Pages serves files, not rules: there is no .htaccess or redirect map.
  A page whose URL has moved therefore needs a real file at the old path that
  sends the reader on. This does it two ways so it works regardless of how
  the request arrives:

    - <meta http-equiv="refresh"> for browsers
    - a visible link, so the page still works if the refresh is blocked

  The stub is noindex and carries no canonical: the target can be a relative
  address with a fragment, and a canonical beside noindex sends a search
  engine two contradicting signals.

  Usage: front matter sets `layout: layouts/redirect.njk`, a `permalink` for
  the OLD path, and `redirect_to` for the new one.
#}<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>{{ title | default("Page moved") }} — Chollima Hunter</title>
  <meta http-equiv="refresh" content="0; url={{ redirect_to }}">
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/tokens.css">
</head>
<body>
  <main id="main-content" class="site-main">
    <h1>This page has moved</h1>
    <p>
      It now lives at <a href="{{ redirect_to }}">{{ redirect_to }}</a>.
      It should redirect automatically.
    </p>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
